From: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5) <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: sfp: allow shared MOD_DEF0 GPIO users

The BPI-R4 Pro 8X LAN-side combo path exposes the SFP1 MOD_DEF0 presence
line both to the generic SFP cage and to the MxL86252C DSA-side mux.  The
mux uses the same read-only presence signal to choose between the SFP and
copper PHY channels.

Runtime evidence on the 8X shows the mux probing first and successfully
requesting GPIO69 as a non-exclusive input:

  mxl862xx mdio-bus:10: ds-mux: registered mux for DSA port 13, SFP channel 0
  gpio-581 ( |mxl862xx-ds-mux-mod-) in hi ACTIVE LOW

The later SFP1 probe then fails with -EBUSY because sfp.c requests the
same MOD_DEF0 line as an exclusive GPIOD_IN consumer:

  sfp sfp1: probe with driver sfp failed with error -16

MOD_DEF0 is an input-only module-present signal, so allow it to use the
kernel's existing non-exclusive GPIO consumer mechanism.  Leave the other
SFP GPIOs unchanged: LOS and TX_FAULT are not shared on this board, and
the output/control GPIOs must remain exclusive.

Adapted-by: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5)
---
 drivers/net/phy/sfp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/sfp.c
@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ static const char *gpio_names[] = {
 };
 
 static const enum gpiod_flags gpio_flags[] = {
-	GPIOD_IN,
+	GPIOD_IN | GPIOD_FLAGS_BIT_NONEXCLUSIVE,
 	GPIOD_IN,
 	GPIOD_IN,
 	GPIOD_ASIS,
